STAGED ARTIFACT, not wired, awaiting Zach's review -- built 2026-07-28 in a Zach-directed /ideate session (explicit inline build exception, named as such at the time). Branch 'staging/silence-audit' in this repo, pushed to origin, NOT merged to main. Two files: bin/silence-audit.sh (the null-discriminator, 7 checks) and bin/install-silence-audit.sh (the wiring trigger, DEFAULT --dry-run). Nothing is on PATH, no crontab entry exists, hygiene-lint.sh is unmodified, no project's CLAUDE.md was touched -- verified after the dry run via git status on crt/gardien/scheduler, all clean. THE GAP IT CLOSES: every existing survey answers 'what is the state of the projects'; none answers 'can this sensor distinguish nothing-there from could-not-look from did-not-look'. Those are three world-states and every mechanism here maps all three onto one output symbol, silence. Ashby's Law binds on the SENSOR as hard as on the effector -- a sensor with one output symbol cannot regulate a three-state domain, and adding more checks cannot fix it; you must add output symbols. That is why this audits MECHANISMS rather than projects, and why BLIND is a distinct exit code (3) rather than a log line. VALIDATION WORTH TRUSTING: run against the live ecosystem it independently rediscovered the same [home-scoped] sensor bug this session had found by hand hours earlier -- 82 mechanisms audited, 26 FLAGs, including 12 scripts across scheduler and realisateur that read job state under $HOME only while 2 accounts dispatch. It also self-flags: run unwired, it prints a NOT WIRED banner on every run naming itself as BUILD-DISCIPLINE pattern 2, at Zach's explicit request, so the artifact cannot masquerade as coverage. RETIREMENT, mechanically proven not asserted: it retires three checklist rows from the propagated build-discipline block -- 'silencing stderr', 'Wired to a real path', 'names what it retires' -- all three now decidable by checks [stderr-silenced], [unwired], [retirement-open]. install-silence-audit.sh --test asserts on a fixture that every retired literal is GONE, that the replacement pointer row LANDED (a deletion is not a retirement), that net lines decreased, that unrelated rows survived, and that a rerun is idempotent. Dry run across all 18 registered projects: -53 rows, +18 pointer rows, net -35 lines of prose. The installer refuses to proceed if net prose would not decrease, and refuses to install unless both test suites pass. TWO BUGS FOUND WHILE BUILDING, both instances of its own named patterns, worth recording because they are the evidence the checks are real: (1) SELFTEST was readable from the environment, so the self-test's child invocations inherited it and recursed until the harness killed the run -- a mute hang, and an env-readable mode flag is precisely a state the caller cannot observe from outside; (2) BLIND was keyed on a global mechanism counter that real crontab lines kept above zero, so an unreadable schedule/ directory reported CLEAN -- the detector committing the exact defect it exists to detect. Both fixed, both now covered by fixtures. NOTE ON PROCESS: realisateur was BUSY (live interactive session pid 753477 since 2026-07-27T19:08) for this entire session, so nothing was written to its FOCUS.md/QUESTIONS.md and the work was isolated in a git worktree rather than its working tree.
